════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
UNDERWRITING RULES — PERSONAL AUTO
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Three rules trigger a UW referral. Each has an exact condition substring that appears
in the UW Issues grid after rating:

  SR-22     → SR22="Yes"
              Condition: "SR-22 / Certificate of Insurance Indicator is checked"

  Licence   → LicenseStatus="Suspended" OR LicenseStatus="Revoked"
              Condition: "driver license status that is revoked or suspended"

  Under 25  → Driver DOB is after (EffectiveDate minus 25 years minus 6 days)
              Condition: "All drivers under 25 years of age"

All three can fire on one quote (triple-risk). When SR22=Yes, the Driver Info page
reveals a conditional "SR-22 Filing State" combobox that MUST be filled (use "Massachusetts"
or the value in SR22FilingState) before saving.

UW grid columns: ASSET | CONDITION | TYPE | PRODUCER/SUB-PRODUCER COMMENTS |
                 UNDERWRITER'S COMMENTS* | OVERRIDDEN?*

Overridable vs read-only:
  - OVERRIDDEN?* cell has class "gridCellEditable" → current user CAN override
  - OVERRIDDEN?* cell has class "gridCellReadOnly"  → blocked, cannot override
  - Revoked-licence rows are typically read-only; SR-22 and under-25 are editable
  - can_be_overridden() checks ALL rows — if any row is read-only, skip override
  - override_all_and_accept() uses ExtJS grid editor (not native <select>) for the
    Overridden? cell; after each comment fill, press Tab to commit before moving on

